OL,3,CWho was the Godmother of Rock 'n' Roll
OL,4,CSister Rosetta Tharpe?
OL,6,FSister Rosetta's influence on the
OL,7,Fgenre is immeasurable: decades before
OL,8,Fthe likes of Elvis Presley, Chuck
OL,9,FBerry, or Little Richard took to the
OL,10,Fstage, she was already thrilling
OL,11,Faudiences with her electrifying guitar
OL,12,Fwork and gospel-infused vocals.
OL,14,FDespite her groundbreaking
OL,15,Fcontributions, Sister Rosetta's place
OL,16,Fin popular music history is frequently
OL,17,Foverlooked.
OL,19,FYet, her legacy continues to inspire
OL,20,Fmusicians around the world.
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G2/7
OL,2,W/*%+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,
